---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: A small web clubhouse
description: Notes, resources and a neighbourly webring for people making homes on the open web.
---
<section class="hero h-card">
  <div class="hero__copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Broadcasting from our own little corner</p>
    <h1 class="p-name">Make the web <span>yours.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero__lede p-note">hckr.lol is a living example of an independent website: hand-tended with Eleventy, published as plain files, and ready to move anywhere.</p>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="button button--signal" href="/resources/getting-started/">Start your own site →</a>
      <a class="button" href="/colophon/">How this one works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% set meetup = events | nextEvent %}
  <aside class="hero__panel" aria-label="Next meetup">
    {% for event in events | publishedEvents %}
    <div class="hero__panel-content" data-next-event data-event-end="{{ event.end }}"{% if not meetup or meetup.date != event.date %} hidden{% endif %}>
      <p class="hero__panel-label">Next transmission / {{ event.title }}</p>
      <div>
        <time datetime="{{ event.start }}">{{ event.date | eventDay }}<br>{{ event.date | eventMonth }}</time>
        <p>{{ event.startTime }}–{{ event.endTime }}<br>{{ event.location }}</p>
      </div>
      <p class="broadcast"><a href="/events/">Details</a> · <a href="{{ event.ticketUrl }}">Tickets →</a></p>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
    <div class="hero__panel-content" data-next-event-soon{% if meetup %} hidden{% endif %}>
      <p class="hero__panel-label">Next transmission</p>
      <p>The next meetup is coming soon. Come back soon to get tickets.</p>
      <p class="broadcast"><a href="/events/">Past meetups →</a></p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</section>

<div class="ticker" aria-hidden="true">
  <p>OWN YOUR URL ✦ WRITE SOMETHING WEIRD ✦ VIEW SOURCE ✦ JOIN THE RING ✦ SMALL WEB, BIG FEELINGS ✦&nbsp; OWN YOUR URL ✦ WRITE SOMETHING WEIRD ✦ VIEW SOURCE ✦ JOIN THE RING ✦ SMALL WEB, BIG FEELINGS ✦&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<section class="section-shell" aria-labelledby="explore-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Three doors, no algorithm</p>
      <h2 id="explore-heading">Wander around</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="explore-grid">
    <a class="explore-card" href="/blog/">
      <span>01 / Field notes</span>
      <h3>Things we are learning in public</h3>
      <p>Short essays about owning URLs, tending sites and making software legible.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="explore-card" href="/resources/">
      <span>02 / The handbook</span>
      <h3>A pocket guide to the IndieWeb</h3>
      <p>Small, linked explanations of the standards and practices behind independent sites.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="explore-card" href="/webring/">
      <span>03 / Neighbours</span>
      <h3>Take a lap around the webring</h3>
      <p>No feed-ranking machinery. Just people pointing to the next interesting person.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-shell" aria-labelledby="latest-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Fresh from the notebook</p>
      <h2 id="latest-heading">Latest notes</h2>
    </div>
    <a href="/blog/">All notes →</a>
  </div>
  <ol class="post-list">
    {% for post in collections.posts | head(3) %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ post.url }}">
          <time datetime="{{ post.date | htmlDateString }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time>
          <h3>{{ post.data.title }}</h3>
          <span class="post-list__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>
